  "final_answer": "I have found the answer. Looking at the M5 Pro chip options that appeared after clicking it, I can clearly see two GPU configurations available.\n\n## Answer\n\n**Yes**, the Mac mini can be configured with a GPU larger than 16-core.\n\nOn the Mac mini buy page (`apple.com/shop/buy-mac/mac-mini`), when configuring the **M5 Pro chip**, there are two options available:\n\n1. **M5 Pro (default):** 15-core CPU, **16-core GPU** — Included\n2. **M5 Pro (boost):** 18-core CPU, **20-core GPU** — Upgrade option (\"Boost your processing and...\")\n\nSo the M5 Pro chip can be configured with a **20-core GPU**, which is larger than 16-core.\n\nFor reference, the alternative **M6 chip** is only available with a 12-core GPU (no larger GPU option is offered for the M6). Only the M5 Pro chip allows a GPU upgrade beyond 16-core (specifically to 20-core).",
